Let $x_{ij}$ denote the quantity of goods transported from distribution center $i$ to customer group $j$.

**Sets:**
- $i \in \{\text{S1}, \text{S2}, \text{S3}, \text{S4}, \text{S5}, \text{S6}, \text{S7}, \text{S8}, \text{S9}, \text{S10}, \text{S11}, \text{S12}, \text{S13}, \text{S14}, \text{S15}, \text{S16}, \text{S17}, \text{S18}\}$
- $j \in \{\text{C1}, \text{C2}, \text{C3}, \text{C4}, \text{C5}, \text{C6}, \text{C7}, \text{C8}, \text{C9}, \text{C10}, \text{C11}, \text{C12}, \text{C13}, \text{C14}, \text{C15}, \text{C16}, \text{C17}, \text{C18}\}$

**Parameters:**
- $c_{ij}$: Transportation cost per unit from distribution center $i$ to customer group $j$ (see table below)
- $d_j$: Demand of customer group $j$
